{# ============================================================================
   THE ROSTER'S OVERVIEW TAB — the design's modules/roster/index.html.

   THE TAB IS COMPOSED, NOT DRAWN. The design's own `.w-grid` is empty in the
   source for the same reason this block is a loop: which widgets, how wide
   and in what order comes from the shell's widget framework resolving
   RosterWidgets, and the shipped composition is what a person who has never
   chosen sees — the figures, what needs a decision, the posts and who the
   pings put on them, the plate.

   THE WIDGETS THEMSELVES live in _w_<id>.html.twig and are rendered by BOTH
   this page and the widget library, so a library preview IS the widget.

   EDITING NEVER HAPPENS HERE. Add, remove, width and order are the library's,
   reached by the one standard door every module ships.
   ========================================================================== #}
{% extends '@UhifadhiRoster/base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}{{ area.name }} · Roster{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}Roster{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_subtitle %}
    {%- set stations = roster_url(constant('Uhifadhi\\Bundle\\AreaBundle\\Controller\\StationsController::ROUTE'), {uuid: area.uuid}) -%}
    Who is due, who checked in, and where their handset says they actually are. The stations and the live positions are the
    {%- if stations %} <a href="{{ stations }}">area&rsquo;s</a>{% else %} area&rsquo;s{% endif %}.
{% endblock %}

{% block roster_page %}
    {{ include('@UhifadhiRoster/_identity_band.html.twig') }}

    {# THE LIBRARY DOOR IS NOT HERE YET, and a door to a screen that does not
       exist is worse than none. The surface is composed and the framework
       resolves it; what is missing is the module's own library page — the
       one standard `.tgl.w-act` link goes in exactly here when it lands. #}

    <div class="w-grid">
        {% for widget in widgets %}
            {% if widget.on %}
                <div data-w="{{ widget.id }}" class="w-cell w-span-{{ widget.cols }}">
                    <div class="w-inner">
                        {{ include('@UhifadhiRoster/dashboard/_w_' ~ widget.id ~ '.html.twig') }}
                    </div>
                </div>
            {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
{% endblock %}
